# vLLM checkpoint-aware KV-cache dtype rollout

Memory type: playbook
Recorded: 2026-08-04T04:27:00.634162+00:00
Confidence: 0.98
Owner: Jamal Pierce
Tags: vllm, issue-34752, kv-cache, fp8, private-deployment, rollback

## Summary

For vLLM issue #34752, resolve KV-cache dtype before backend/cache construction. If supported checkpoint kv_cache_quant_algo exists, omitted or explicit auto selects it; an explicit matching/equivalent dtype is allowed; an incompatible explicit override fails configuration with corrective flags. Without metadata, auto and explicit behavior remain unchanged. Validate every GPU family, canary on matching hardware, and roll back to the prior image/model/config while rebuilding incompatible caches.

## Outcome

Implemented and CPU-validated on pinned vLLM source; indexed code, tests, and private-deployment rollout runbook.

